{"guide":{"questionsToConsider":["Who answers media requests, and do they need the phone number as well as the email?","Which spokespeople are available, and should the form list them by name?","Do you have a media kit you can link to in the ending, so asset requests answer themselves?","What is your policy on filming at your premises?"],"howToUseResponses":"Sort new requests by deadline, since a same-day quote needs a reply within hours while a feature can wait a few days. Tell the journalist early if you can't help, because a clear no lets them move on. Keep a record of outlets and topics in an exported CSV, which becomes your press list for future announcements.","customizeSteps":["List your actual spokespeople or press contacts in the interview follow-up if you want to steer requests.","Add a link to your media kit in the ending so asset requests can be served straight away.","Link the form from the press or newsroom page on your site, or embed it there directly."],"faqs":[{"q":"What should a media request form ask?","a":"The journalist's contact details, the outlet, what they want, the story angle and the deadline. The deadline matters most, because press requests are time-sensitive."},{"q":"Where should I put a media request form?","a":"On your press or newsroom page, and in the signature of whoever handles press. Journalists look there first for a direct route."},{"q":"Should I ask for the journalist's phone number?","a":"Yes, if you can call back. Tight deadlines are often resolved faster by phone than by email."},{"q":"Can I use this for event press passes too?","a":"Yes. Copy the template with Use this template, add a request type for press passes and a follow-up asking which event and date."}]},"doc":{"schemaVersion":9,"title":"Media request","description":"Collect press enquiries with everything your communications team needs to respond.","blocks":[{"id":"blk_mediareq00","ref":"welcome","title":"Hello. Tell us about your story and we'll get back to you b